  "checks": [
    "CodeEdit and TextEdit snapshots update the arranged scroll model under an XUI call scope; only a successful measurement publishes the independent result.",
    "The terminal clamps absolute and relative pixel offsets. Effective changes invalidate the render cache, including fractional offsets, and an unchanged or invalid offset retains existing state.",
    "Scrolling up preserves history across new output. Returning to the latest row restores tail following. The native terminal regression verifies three-row wheel movement against the same model.",
    "The copied values remain readable after widget and Context retirement. The C generation check verifies the direct native calls, and static AOT has no XGE host-library import.",
    "The terminal history example renders text with both JIT and static AOT. The separate fixture checks the scroll operations and follow behavior."
  ],
  "costs": [
    "Each snapshot transfers one fixed-size native value. CodeEdit and TextEdit keep the native layout and measurement work, including any allocations required by the existing layout path.",
    "The managed bindings use the existing owner-view scope and checked status conversion. No new compiler/runtime wrapper or source-level dispatch is introduced.",
    "The warmed paired terminal test alternates a vertical delta of +8 and -8 pixels for 100 effective changes in each path. Counters cover XRT alloc/free/realloc and exclude rendering and timing."
  ],
